• **Task 1 (#1008, product):** `yoyo commit "two words"` should commit exactly the message the user typed. Before fixing commit, the agent first checks every shell command that goes through the same argument-quoting step, by running each one, to find others that leak quotes.
  • The rule to hold: the commit subject matches the user's message byte for byte. Quotes inside a message, like say "hi" now, are kept.
  • It also confirms the REPL's /commit add f still commits add f.
  • Simply switching the parser to the quote-stripping tokenizer is ruled out, because it would eat those inner quotes.
  • The tests run the real binary against real git. The commit message carries Fixes #1008.
